title: The Barons revolt!
subtitle: What is even going on within the PSOE?
new-page: true
face-image: img/events/barones_revolt.jpg
on-arrival: {!
    if (!Q.psoe_barons_revolted) {
        Q.psoe_barons_revolted = true; // the revolt happens even if Sánchez holds on
        G.spaSupportInject(Q, Q.congreso_left_carrier, 'all', 1.5, 'psoe');
        G.spaSupportInject(Q, 'abstain', 'all', 1.0, 'psoe');
    }
    Q.psoe_holdout_possible = Q.player_party == 'erc' && !Q.psc_split
        && Q.psoe_leader == 'Pedro Sánchez' && !Q.congreso_coalition_sorpasso
        && !Q.psoe_holdout_congress && !this.state.visits['psoe_primaries_2017']
        && Q.psc_relations >= (Q.difficulty > 0 ? 75 : 65)
        && Q[Q.parlament_current_icv + '_relations'] >= (Q.difficulty > 0 ? 65 : 55)
        && Q.party_resources >= 2;
!}

= The Barons revolt!

It's no secret that the Barons of the PSOE have now been long time dissatisfied with the leadership of Pedro Sánchez. Now, with an impossible arithmetic in the Congreso and with the open support of former Presidente Felipe González, they have gathered unprecedented momentum within the party. It seems that the only card that Pero Sánchez can try to play before being ousted as Secretary-General is to call for a primary election before that, where he could potentially re-validate his leadership. Yet it does not seem likely to happen unless his now-limited regional allies can come together in time.

- @happens
- @holdout

@happens
title: The Barons force Sánchez to resign
on-arrival: {!
    if (Q.psoe_barons_revolted && !Q.psoe_holdout_congress && Q.psoe_leader == 'Pedro Sánchez') {
        Q.congreso_coalition_grand_ok = true;
        Q.psoe_leadership_mult = -0.5;
        Q.psoe_leader = "???";
        Q.psoe_leader_gender = "f";
        G.setText(Q, "psoe_ideology", G.text("Centrist Social Democracy, Autonomism"));
        Q.psoe_party_congres_countdown = 12;
        if (!Q.countdowns.includes("psoe_party_congres")) Q.countdowns.push("psoe_party_congres");
    }
!}

In what can only be categorized as an internal coup, the Barons of the PSOE have now ousted Pedro Sánchez. The party is set to be ruled by an interim council until new a new primary election is held, leaving the question of coalition negotiations in an impossible-to-resolve limbo.

- @congreso_coalition: So what's the PSOE going to do?

@holdout
title: Can we give any sort of support for Perdo Sánchez to hold on?
view-if: {! return Q.player_party == "erc" && !this.state.visits['psoe_primaries_2017']; !}
choose-if: psoe_holdout_possible
subtitle: The PSC would need some extra help if that strategy is to have any chance of working out, both from us and from other leftist parties willing to lend a hand. \[-2 resources\]
unavailable-subtitle: [? if psc_split: The PSC is no longer a part of the PSOE's federal structure, so we really have no avenue to help out. ?][? if congreso_coalition_sorpasso: With the PSOE reaching unprecedented lows electorally, Pedro Sánchez has really no support to hold on to. ?][? if (difficulty <= 0 and psc_relations < 65) or (difficulty > 0 and psc_relations < 75): Our relations with the PSC are not good enough. ?][? if {! return (Q[Q.parlament_current_icv + '_relations'] || 0) < (Q.difficulty > 0 ? 65 : 55); !}: Our relations with [+ parlament_current_icv +] are not good enough. ?][? if party_resources < 2: Not enough resources. ?]
on-arrival: {!
    if (Q.psoe_barons_revolted && Q.psoe_holdout_possible && !Q.psoe_holdout_congress
        && Q.player_party == 'erc' && !Q.psc_split && Q.psoe_leader == 'Pedro Sánchez'
        && !Q.congreso_coalition_sorpasso && !this.state.visits['psoe_primaries_2017']
        && Q.psc_relations >= (Q.difficulty > 0 ? 75 : 65)
        && Q[Q.parlament_current_icv + '_relations'] >= (Q.difficulty > 0 ? 65 : 55)
        && Q.party_resources >= 2) {
        Q.party_resources -= 2;
        Q.psoe_holdout_congress = true;
        Q.congreso_coalition_grand_ok = false;
        Q.psoe_party_congres_trigger = false;
        Q.psoe_party_congres_countdown = 1;
        if (!Q.countdowns.includes('psoe_party_congres')) Q.countdowns.push('psoe_party_congres');
    }
!}
go-to: congreso_coalition_barons if not psoe_holdout_congress

In a political drama only paralleled by movies, Pedro Sánchez has been able to recuperate his standing thanks to his alliances in the semi-independent parties that form the federal structure of the PSOE. Chief amongst them, the PSC, the faction that has pushed the hardest for an immediate vote of confidence for the Secretary-General among the party members. We'll now have to see who emerges from this extraordinary vote.

- @await_primary: Continue...

@await_primary
on-arrival: {!
    if (Q.psoe_holdout_congress && !this.state.visits['psoe_primaries_2017'] && Q.psoe_party_congres_countdown > 0) {
        Q.month_actions = Math.max(Q.month_actions || 0, 1);
    }
!}
go-to: post_event
